    {
      "_highlightResult": {
        "author": {
          "matchLevel": "none",
          "matchedWords": [],
          "value": "fidla"
        },
        "story_text": {
          "fullyHighlighted": false,
          "matchLevel": "full",
          "matchedWords": [
            "urban",
            "air",
            "pollution"
          ],
          "value": "at any given time over a major metropolitan city (and NYC is the largest in the US), there will be any or all of the following types of airborne products:<p>Human-Operated Airborne Products:<p>Commercial Airliners\nGeneral Aviation Aircraft\nPrivate Planes\nCharter Flights\nCargo Planes\nBusiness Jets\nHelicopters\nNews Helicopters\nMedical Evacuation (Medevac) Helicopters\nPolice, Fire, and Rescue Helicopters\nTour and Sightseeing Helicopters\nTraining Aircraft\nAerial Advertising Planes\nAgricultural Aircraft\nMilitary Aircraft\nAerial Survey Planes\nVIP Transport\nGliders\nUltralights<p>Delivery Drones and VTOL/eVTOL:\nAmazon Prime <em>Air</em>\nWalmart Delivery Drones\nUPS Flight Forward\nZipline\nFlytrex\nWisk Aero\nArcher Aviation\nBeta Technologies\nVolocopter\nElroy <em>Air</em><p>Scientific and Testing Balloons:\nCollege/University Scientific Balloons: Used for atmospheric research, <em>air</em> quality testing, etc.\n<em>Urban</em> <em>Air</em> Quality Testing Balloons: For monitoring <em>pollution</em> levels in metropolitan areas.\nAdvertising and Non-Winged Craft:<p>Advertising Balloons: Large, floating banners or shapes for promotional activities.\nTethered Aerostats: Used by agencies like U.S. Customs and Border Protection for surveillance.<p>High-Altitude Surveillance Balloons: Including those used for military or security purposes.\nHot <em>Air</em> Balloons: For tourism, advertising, or personal enjoyment.<p>Weather Balloons: Released by weather services and research institutions for meteorological data."
        },
        "title": {
          "matchLevel": "none",
          "matchedWords": [],
          "value": "Drones / Aliens over NJ"
        }
      },
